// Live collision bake: data/stageCollision.json, generated by
// tools/liteaudit/stage_bake.py. All 29 vanilla VS IDs have explicit coverage.
// collisionGeometry uses true Slippi frames (dump match_frame), current
// line kinds and stepwise visibility. Only observed complete loops repeat.
// Random/player-triggered pieces retain fallbacks pending stageSim ports;
// STAGE_COVERAGE exposes the bounds and partial/legacy status. Decorative main
// polygons never determine baked floor truth. See tools/liteaudit/README.md.
//
// Historical authored-geometry provenance (retained fallbacks below):
// Melee stage geometry keyed by INTERNAL stage id. Main outline polygon +
// side platforms; +y is up. The 6 legal stages are ported from slippilab
// components/viewer/Stage.tsx (MIT). FoD platforms use initial heights
// (per-frame heights not carried yet); Yoshi's moving Randall platform is
// drawn via randallPlatform below.
//
// Non-legal stages were extracted from the vanilla stage DATs' SBM_Coll_Data
// (vertex + line tables, grouped by MapJoint), scaled by grGroundParam's
// stage scale, with jobj-attached collision groups placed via the coll-joint
// -> map-gobj links (the map_head group link lists in the DAT + the DOL
// StageData x2C tables read from the vanilla main.dol). The link's node
// index walks the group's jobj tree with z=0 AT THE GROUP ROOT (the game
// hands mpLib_800552B0 the grGroundParam scale-wrapper jobj, so the walk
// starts at its child = the group root; see Ground_801C1A20 /
// Ground_801C2ED0 in the decomp). A few placements are code-driven and
// mirrored here: Great Bay's turtle home (grGreatBay_801F4694: kame_x+46,
// kame_y-9). Every entry was validated against grounded fighter positions
// sampled from real replays (>=90% of grounded samples within ~3 units of a
// floor surface, moving pieces excluded).
//
// The original entries carried only static/neutral geometry: continuously moving or
// anim-parked pieces (Fourside's UFO + crane + helicopter, Great Bay's
// Tingle balloon, Green Greens star blocks, MK II's pit platforms + coin
// blocks, Venom's arwings, Kongo Jungle N64's circulating platforms, Flat
// Zone's G&W tool copies beyond their parked spots, Peach's Castle see-saw
// sag) are omitted; the Great Bay turtle IS carried at its parked home.
// Corneria (7) is carried at the Great Fox's base pose (0, 250): the ship
// random-walks within +-20 units of it (grCorneria_801E1970 + the DAT's
// yakumono_param limits) but never leaves that envelope; the flyby arwings
// are omitted movers. Because the WHOLE ship drifts, its entry is marked
// `anchored: true` — litePaint infers a per-frame vertical offset from
// grounded fighter positions (via surfaceYAt below) and shifts the drawn
// geometry to match. Measured on real replays: static error median ~8 units
// (residuals wander -13..+18 with the random walk), <2.5 after anchoring.
// The other non-legal stages were measured the same way and their grounded
// samples sit dead-on the base pose (medians ~0) — static is correct there,
// so nothing else is anchored. Stages whose core layout is animated are omitted
// entirely: Kongo Jungle (5, bobbing main platform), Brinstar Depths (15,
// whole stage rotates) and the scrolling stages (10, 11, 24, 25) which use
// the ground-plane fallback. Poke Floats (23) has no static geometry but
// gets animated movers via moverSegments() below (baked joint-animation
// tracks in meleeMovers.json).
